  "summary": "Belmont City Council held a June 27 special meeting to consider adopting Flock automated license plate reader cameras, with police citing crime-solving benefits and a majority of councilmembers supportive but seeking stronger oversight and policy safeguards before moving forward. Vice Mayor Hurt said she could not support the policy as written, and Mayor Mates suggested annual outside audits; the council agreed to refer implementation details to the Public Safety Subcommittee.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "As the policy is written, I can't support it. I think there is a lot more work that has to be done for robust oversight.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "Belmont Police Chief Ken Stenquist noted the city would keep data information private from Texas and other states after questions from the council about state policing agencies getting data of women who come to California for public health reasons.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "I think if we are going to go ahead and move further on this, we really need to ensure the policy we have in place has the guardrails that reflect the values of this community",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
